values
  ('p-estherformula-ceramide-strips', 'ESTHER FORMULA Esther Lyuh Ceramide Strips (Hyaluronic Acid & Ceramide)', 'ESTHER FORMULA', 'supplement', 'physical', 'Apple-flavored strips that dissolve on the roof of the mouth, from the Korean supplement brand ESTHER FORMULA. Each strip has 960 mcg of plant ceramides (activeCera, fermented from fruit and vegetable extract), 90 mg of hyaluronic acid (Hi-Aqua) and 10 mg of gotu kola extract. The brand says it supports skin hydration, elasticity and the skin barrier. 15 individually wrapped strips. Vegan and sugar-free; sweetened with aspartame.', '$24.99 on Amazon (15 strips)', 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51q39aFdEdL._AC_SL500_.jpg', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQN7VN4R', '["esther formula","esther lyuh","skin","hydration","ceramide","hyaluronic acid","gotu kola","oral strip","k-beauty","beauty supplement","supplement"]'::jsonb, '["supplement","skin-hair"]'::jsonb, '["Amazon","Olive Young US"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Sold as a dietary supplement, which the FDA does not evaluate for safety or efficacy. The listing says its statements have not been evaluated by the FDA.","materials":"15 individually wrapped oral strips, 0.3 g each (4.5 g total). Manufacturer listed on Amazon as ESTHER FORMULA USA Corporation; country of manufacture not stated on the pages read.","recalls":"No recalls found.","sideEffects":"Contains phenylalanine (from aspartame), which matters for people with phenylketonuria (PKU). For adults only; check with a doctor before use if pregnant, nursing, taking medication or managing a medical condition (per Olive Young US). Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"The \"clinically proven\" numbers (+60% hydration, +35% or +50% elasticity) come from trials of the activeCera ingredient, footnoted as 12 people over 8 weeks, not of these strips, and ayna couldn''t find that trial published. The listing''s images give two different elasticity numbers and two different doses (1 to 2 strips vs 1 to 4 strips a day). No study of this product was found."}'::jsonb, 'ESTHER FORMULA says these strips support skin hydration, elasticity and the skin barrier. Its listing shows "clinically proven" gains of 60% in hydration and 35% in elasticity, but its own footnotes say those come from an 8-week trial of the activeCera ingredient in 12 people, not of these strips. ayna couldn''t find that trial published, and the listing doesn''t say whether it had a placebo group. A separate +50% skin barrier protein figure is footnoted as a cell-culture (lab) study, and the claim that the strip absorbs through the mouth lining is footnoted as lab and rat work on hyaluronic acid only. No study of this product was found.

There is some broader research on oral skin supplements. A 2022 meta-analysis of 66 randomized trials found that oral ceramides and oral hyaluronan both improved skin hydration compared with placebo in healthy adults, and that ceramides also reduced water loss through the skin. Those trials used other ceramide and hyaluronan products at their own doses, so they show what the ingredients can do, not that this product does. One of the four authors worked for a pharmaceutical company.', 'Rated 4.4 out of 5 from 63 ratings on Amazon (75% five-star, 8% four-star, 7% three-star, 1% two-star, 9% one-star). Reviewers mostly mention easy use, taste and softer, more hydrated skin; one 4-star reviewer said results weren''t dramatic, and a 3-star reviewer said the strips were stale and crunchy. At least one top review was an Amazon Vine review of a free product.', 'Oral ceramides and hyaluronan improved skin hydration in a meta-analysis of randomized trials of other products. No study of these strips was found.', 'independent', 'ayna summary of a peer-reviewed meta-analysis of oral skin-moisturizing supplements. Not a direct clinician quote; no study of this product was found.', 'curated', false, false, 4.4, true, '{"userRatingSourceUrl":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQN7VN4R","whereToBuyLinks":{"Amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQN7VN4R","Olive Young US":"https://us.oliveyoung.com/products/UA99304443"},"ingredients":"Supplement Facts per strip (0.3 g), from the Amazon listing images: Ceramides (from Fruits and Vegetable Extract) 960 mcg, Hyaluronic Acid 90 mg, Gotu Kola Extract 10 mg, Sodium 5 mg, 0 calories. Other ingredients per Olive Young US: Pullulan, Calcium Lactate, Beta-Cyclodextrin, Fruit and Vegetable Extract, Glycerin, Hydroxypropyl Methylcellulose, Citric Acid, Aspartame, Apple Flavor.","doctorOpinionShort":"Oral ceramides and hyaluronan improved skin hydration in a 2022 meta-analysis of randomized trials. The brand''s own numbers come from a 12-person ingredient trial ayna couldn''t find published. No study of this product was found.","doctorOpinionCitations":[{"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQN7VN4R","label":"Amazon: ESTHER FORMULA Hyaluronic Acid & Ceramide Strips, ingredients and claims"},{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35719159/","label":"PubMed: Effectiveness of dietary supplements for skin moisturizing in healthy adults, systematic review and meta-analysis of RCTs (Front Nutr, 2022)","chipLabel":"Oral skin supplements meta-analysis, 66 trials (2022)"}],"whoItsFor":["Adults with dry or dehydrated skin who want to try an oral supplement alongside topical care","People who prefer a dissolving strip to capsules","Not for people with phenylketonuria (PKU): it contains aspartame"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per ESTHER FORMULA on Amazon. The listing gives two different amounts: the text says 1 to 4 strips daily, and the how-to image says 1 to 2 daily for maintenance.","steps":["Place one strip on the roof of your mouth.","Let it dissolve completely. No water needed.","Take 1 to 2 strips a day (image) or up to 4 (listing text); check the box you receive."],"sourceUrl":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQN7VN4R","sourceLabel":"Amazon: ESTHER FORMULA Ceramide Strips"},"warnings":["Phenylketonurics: contains phenylalanine (aspartame).","For adults only. Keep out of reach of children.","Pregnant, nursing, taking medication, or managing a medical condition: check with a doctor before use."],"ingredientScienceNote":"These results come from trials of other oral ceramide and hyaluronan products. This product''s own figures come from an unpublished ingredient trial.","ingredientScience":[{"name":"Oral ceramides and hyaluronan","text":"A 2022 systematic review and meta-analysis of 66 randomized controlled trials in healthy adults found oral ceramides increased skin hydration and reduced water loss through the skin compared with placebo, and oral hyaluronan increased skin hydration (too few trials to judge water loss). All the supplements studied were safe over the trial periods, usually 24 weeks or less. One author worked for a pharmaceutical company.","citations":[{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35719159/","label":"PubMed: Effectiveness of dietary supplements for skin moisturizing in healthy adults (Front Nutr, 2022)"}]},{"name":"activeCera (brand-cited trial)","text":"ESTHER FORMULA cites an 8-week human trial of 12 people for its +60% hydration and +35% elasticity figures. The trial tested the activeCera ingredient, not these strips, and ayna couldn''t find it published in PubMed.","citations":[{"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQN7VN4R","label":"Amazon: ESTHER FORMULA listing images and footnotes"}]}],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35719159/","text":"Oral skin-moisturizing supplements, meta-analysis (2022)","summary":"66 trials; oral ceramides and hyaluronan improved hydration. Not this product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"website","url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQN7VN4R","text":"Amazon: ESTHER FORMULA Ceramide Strips reviews","summary":"4.4 out of 5 from 63 ratings on Amazon."},{"platform":"website","url":"https://us.oliveyoung.com/products/UA99304443","text":"Olive Young US: Esther Lyuh Ceramide Strips","summary":"Retailer page with the full ingredient list and warnings."}]}},"integrations":[],"badges":[],"isEmergingBrand":true}'::jsonb)
